@startuml recovery-state
title Fault recovery — parallel state machines (receiver detection || replica role)

skinparam shadowing false
hide empty description

state "Recovery runs as two concurrent state machines" as SYS {

  state "Receiver: per-service failover generation" as RX {
    [*] --> HEALTHY
    HEALTHY --> SUSPECT : missed in [1, missedCount)
    SUSPECT --> FAILED  : missed >= missedCount\n/ bump epoch, send Promote(epoch)
    FAILED  --> FAILED  : still missing\n/ resend same epoch (capped)
    SUSPECT --> HEALTHY : beat
    FAILED  --> HEALTHY : beat (service recovered)
  }

  --

  state "Replica: role (one critical-service instance)" as ROLE {
    [*] --> BACKUP : replica.role = backup
    BACKUP  --> PRIMARY : acceptPromotion(epoch > lastHandledEpoch)
    PRIMARY --> PRIMARY : ignore stale / duplicate Promote
  }
}

note bottom of SYS
  The coupling: the receiver's SUSPECT -> FAILED edge mints the epoch
  that the backup's BACKUP -> PRIMARY transition consumes. The backup
  acts on each epoch once, so the receiver's loss-tolerant resends never
  cause a second promotion. Epoch 0 is the pre-failover value; the first
  real promotion is epoch 1. A replica configured as primary starts in
  PRIMARY and only ever ignores Promotes.
end note

@enduml
